===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|select|or}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-selector.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛktə(ɹ)|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone or something which [[select]]s or [[choose]]s.
#* '''1949''', ''Billboard'' (volume 61, number 34, page 97)
#*: There is one selection for hot chocolate. All '''selectors''' are the push button type.
# {{lb|en|cricket}} An [[administrator]] responsible for selecting which [[player]]s will [[play]] for a [[side]].
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[match]]ing [[expression]] in a [[stylesheet]] determining which [[element]]s in the [[markup]] are affected by a [[style]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Craig Cook|author2=David Schultz|title=Beginning HTML with CSS and XHTML|publisher=Apress|isbn=9781430203506|page=28
|passage=The ID '''selector''' targets just one element per page, making it much more specific than a class '''selector''' that might target many.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Dino Esposito|title=Microsoft ASP.NET and AJAX|publisher=Microsoft Press|isbn=9780735698253|page=140
|passage=The '''selector''' indicates the query expression to run over the DOM; the context indicates the portion of the DOM from which to run the query.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[pointer]] to a [[structure]] describing a [[segment]] of [[memory]].
#* '''1990''', ''Byte'' (volume 15, issues 11-13, page 256)
#*: Phar Lap executables {{...}} provide a protected-mode '''selector''', 34h, that maps to the first megabyte of physical memory.
#* '''1995''', Lary L. Myers, Keith Weiskamp, ''Amazing 3-D games adventure set'' (page 235)
#*: You will only have to be concerned with DPMI, '''selectors''', and such, if you use Borland C++ in DOS.
# {{lb|en|internet|historical}} A [[text]] [[string]] transmitted to a [[Gopher]] [[server]], identifying the [[resource]] to be retrieved.
#: {{cot|en|URL}}
#* '''1996''', Kenneth H. Rosen, ''UNIX System V, Release 4: An Introduction'', McGraw-Hill Osborne Media, page 438:
#*: Gopher '''selector''' strings are more liberal in makeup than URLs and may contain any characters other than a tab, return, or linefeed.
# {{lb|en|music}} A [[disc jockey]].
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Medicine Ball|artist=Eminem|album=Relapse|year=2009|passage=That's my sector, homosexual dissector / Come again, rewind '''selector'''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Julian Henriques|title=Sonic Bodies|publisher=A&C Black|isbn=9781441144294|page=125
|passage=This sonic body has to decide which music track to play at any particular moment. But when the '''selector''' is alone in front of the crowd, how do they know which track to play next?}}
# {{lb|en|AU|historical}} A person who is entitled to choose a tract of Crown land to purchase.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=78|passage=Each '''selector''' in turn chose the particular allotment he wanted for his client, and so on till this important work was over.}}

